WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.173
The children arrived at the castle and found Mabel's aunt reading a romance novel.

2
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:14.510
"Excuse me," said Gerald, "I believe you've lost your niece."

3
00:00:14.511 --> 00:00:18.142
"I didn't lose Mabel. She left."

4
00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:21.810
"Did you get her note?" asked Kathleen.

5
00:00:21.811 --> 00:00:25.935
"Yes, and I'm happy she's living with a rich lady."

6
00:00:25.936 --> 00:00:29.107
Jimmy couldn't be quiet a moment longer.

7
00:00:29.108 --> 00:00:32.020
He had to tell Mabel's aunt the truth.

8
00:00:32.021 --> 00:00:35.949
"Mabel's invisible! She's standing right beside me."

9
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:40.390
"Don't lie to me!" The aunt glared at Jimmy.

10
00:00:40.391 --> 00:00:42.029
"Please remove this boy.

11
00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.925
I'm quite happy about Mabel."

12
00:00:44.926 --> 00:00:47.723
" Well! "

13
00:00:47.724 --> 00:00:52.720
said Gerald. He was puzzled by this aunt who didn't care about her

14
00:00:52.721 --> 00:00:56.102
missing niece. "But what will Mabel's

15
00:00:56.103 --> 00:01:00.545
parents say?" "Mabel's parents are dead," the aunt

16
00:01:00.546 --> 00:01:04.133
said calmly. The children talked to Mabel's aunt for a few

17
00:01:04.134 --> 00:01:08.272
more minutes. She gave them permission to wander over the

18
00:01:08.273 --> 00:01:12.084
castle grounds. But she still didn't seem concerned

19
00:01:12.085 --> 00:01:16.213
about Mabel. "Good-bye, children," she said and went back to

20
00:01:16.214 --> 00:01:19.535
reading. When the children were outside again, Mabel

21
00:01:19.536 --> 00:01:21.470
said, "I knew she'd believe my

22
00:01:21.471 --> 00:01:23.740
note. She reads lots of romance

23
00:01:23.741 --> 00:01:27.035
novels. Strange things always happen in her

24
00:01:27.036 --> 00:01:31.937
books." Mabel suggested they walk to the Temple of

25
00:01:31.938 --> 00:01:33.788
Flora. When they were seated, she

26
00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:37.456
said, "I'm hungry, and you can't keep stealing food for

27
00:01:37.457 --> 00:01:40.569
me. I'll have to pretend to be a ghost in the

28
00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:46.289
castle." "You must stay with us until you can remove the ring," Kathleen said

29
00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:50.332
kindly. "I think we need to earn some money for food," said

30
00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.998
Mabel. "Let's go to the

31
00:01:51.999 --> 00:01:54.837
fair. Gerald can do magic tricks for

32
00:01:54.838 --> 00:01:58.474
money." "But I don't know any tricks!" said

33
00:01:58.475 --> 00:02:02.569
Gerald. "Don't worry," said Mabel. "I'm

34
00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:05.864
invisible. I can make it look like you're doing

35
00:02:05.865 --> 00:02:08.690
tricks." The fair was about half a mile

36
00:02:08.691 --> 00:02:11.910
away. Soon they could hear music from the

37
00:02:11.911 --> 00:02:17.581
carousel. Kathleen and Jimmy blended into the crowd while Gerald and Mabel stood in front of a

38
00:02:17.582 --> 00:02:21.211
tent. "Ladies and gentlemen," called out

39
00:02:21.212 --> 00:02:25.495
Gerald. "My invisible assistant can make money

40
00:02:25.496 --> 00:02:29.989
disappear." A crowd began to gather, and Kathleen and Jimmy joined

41
00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:33.057
in. Gerald laid nine pennies on the

42
00:02:33.058 --> 00:02:38.291
ground. Mabel picked them up and put them in her pocket to make them

43
00:02:38.292 --> 00:02:40.609
disappear. The audience

44
00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:45.628
clapped. "If you want to see more magic, I'll need to see more money," said

45
00:02:45.629 --> 00:02:48.905
Gerald. The audience dropped more coins onto the

46
00:02:48.906 --> 00:02:51.765
ground. Then Mabel made more things

47
00:02:51.766 --> 00:02:58.213
vanish. Other things appeared to move around by

48
00:02:58.214 --> 00:03:03.050
themselves. "For my final trick, I will vanish!" said

49
00:03:03.051 --> 00:03:07.824
Gerald. He stepped back, and Mabel wrapped her shawl around

50
00:03:07.825 --> 00:03:09.867
him. But nothing

51
00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:12.708
happened. "He can't do it!" someone

52
00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:15.704
yelled. The crowd pushed forward in

53
00:03:15.705 --> 00:03:20.172
anger. "I wish I could put you in my pocket," Mabel whispered to

54
00:03:20.173 --> 00:03:22.060
Gerald. "Then you'd be invisible."

55
00:03:22.061 --> 00:03:24.699
She squeezed her hands together.

56
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.688
"Hey! The ring is loose!"

57
00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:31.090
"Come on!" shouted a man in the crowd.

58
00:03:31.091 --> 00:03:33.695
"We paid for a show."

59
00:03:33.696 --> 00:03:37.100
Gerald whispered to Mabel, "Go into the tent.

60
00:03:37.101 --> 00:03:39.866
Slip the ring under the canvas to me.

61
00:03:39.867 --> 00:03:45.055
When I see you in the crowd, I'll make myself disappear and catch up with you."

62
00:03:45.056 --> 00:03:49.470
Mabel did just that.

63
00:03:49.471 --> 00:03:54.281
"I'm back," she said to a surprised Kathleen and Jimmy.

64
00:03:54.282 --> 00:03:55.910
"Gerald's wearing the ring.

65
00:03:55.911 --> 00:03:58.235
Let's get out of here."

66
00:03:58.236 --> 00:04:07.387
As the children walked away, they heard Gerald announce, "Now I will vanish."

67
00:04:07.388 --> 00:04:13.439
Then the crowd roared, and the children knew he had really disappeared this time.

68
00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:20.476
After a few minutes, they heard footsteps on the road but saw no one.

69
00:04:20.477 --> 00:04:24.077
"Hello, I'm over here," said Gerald.

70
00:04:24.078 --> 00:04:28.457
"Good," said Mabel. "I want my ring back."

71
00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:31.729
"Well, you can't have it," Gerald answered.

72
00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:38.054
"Because I can't get it off!"

